IMPORT prelude

-- South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013 (SA) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. Dates are compared by serial number.
--
-- "21 days from the time the decision-maker receives notice" (regulations r 6) and "within 1 month of the making of the
-- decision" (ss 70(2), 71(3)) are read with the first day excluded. A month is a calendar month, and a period of one
-- month after a day ends on the corresponding day of the next month, or on that month's last day if it has no
-- corresponding day (31 January -> 28 or 29 February). The Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (SA), which would govern
-- how periods are reckoned and whether a last day falling on a weekend or public holiday moves, is not deposited:
-- fork F1 in NOTES.md.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026. CC BY 4.0.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is on or before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b

-- The number of days in a calendar month.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the length of month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The last day of a period of one calendar month after a day: the corresponding day of the next month, or the last
-- day of that month where it has none.
GIVEN `the day of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of one month after` `the day of the event` MEANS
    IF `the day number` AT MOST `the length of month` `the next month` `of` `its year`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY `the day number` `the next month` `its year`
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (`the length of month` `the next month` `of` `its year`) `the next month` `its year`
    WHERE
        `the day number` MEANS DATE_DAY `the day of the event`
        `the next month` MEANS
            IF DATE_MONTH `the day of the event` EQUALS 12
            THEN 1
            ELSE DATE_MONTH `the day of the event` PLUS 1
        `its year` MEANS
            IF DATE_MONTH `the day of the event` EQUALS 12
            THEN DATE_YEAR `the day of the event` PLUS 1
            ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day of the event`
